WEBVTT

00:01.861 --> 00:04.191
shinjitai
I want to believe

00:04.301 --> 00:07.361
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light that I found that day

00:07.841 --> 00:10.571
kimi to kawashita
Because I still have

00:10.571 --> 00:15.241
tatta hitotsuno yakusoku ga arukara
That one promise that I made to you

00:15.641 --> 00:22.641
mou tachidomarazuni aruite yukitai
I want to keep walking, never stopping

00:24.351 --> 00:27.221
Dragon Drive

00:27.221 --> 00:32.681
uresugita kajitsu wo kajiru youni
Like biting into an overripe fruit

00:32.791 --> 00:35.761
yowai jibun ni
I was spoiling myself

00:35.761 --> 00:39.031
amaetsuzukete ita
I was giving in to my weakness

00:39.501 --> 00:43.871
kimi ni deawanakereba
If I hadn't met you

00:43.871 --> 00:45.841
ima mo
I'd still...

00:45.841 --> 00:52.181
kabe wo kowasu koto nado dekinakatta yo
...be unable to break the walls around me

00:53.881 --> 00:56.251
wasurenai
I'll never forget

00:56.251 --> 00:59.481
ano hi kanjita itami
The pain that I felt that day

00:59.791 --> 01:04.861
nido to ano basho modoritakunai
I never want to go back to that place

01:04.861 --> 01:06.451
motto tsuyoku
This strong feeling

01:06.561 --> 01:08.961
shinjitai
I want to believe

01:08.961 --> 01:12.131
ano hi mitsuketa hikari
In the light I found that day

01:12.501 --> 01:17.571
kakkowarui to warawaretemo ii
Let them laugh and call me a loser

01:17.571 --> 01:20.311
bukiyou dakara
Because I'm clumsy

01:20.311 --> 01:28.011
onaji ikikata shika erabenainda
I can only choose to live life this way

01:47.801 --> 01:50.501
Why is that dragon recovering so quickly?

01:50.901 --> 01:53.461
Please. Give it to that child.

01:54.271 --> 01:55.281
H-Hey!

01:55.281 --> 01:56.501
Come on! Hey!

01:56.581 --> 01:58.571
This'll end it!

02:01.721 --> 02:03.081
I won't lose!

02:03.081 --> 02:05.311
I...

02:06.951 --> 02:07.981
Mukai.

02:08.861 --> 02:10.591
Please stop fighting.

02:11.191 --> 02:12.181
Mother.

02:14.961 --> 02:18.091
Eve of the Battle

02:26.941 --> 02:28.201
Mother!

02:28.741 --> 02:30.111
I see that you're awake.

02:32.151 --> 02:33.811
Not to worry.

02:33.811 --> 02:36.151
Your injuries aren't serious.

02:37.121 --> 02:38.851
Did I... lose?

02:39.551 --> 02:41.581
I...

02:42.691 --> 02:45.261
W-Well, yeah, but, you know...

02:45.261 --> 02:46.991
...luck has a lot to do with the outcome.

02:46.991 --> 02:48.361
You almost had me there.

02:48.361 --> 02:49.101
You're right.

02:49.101 --> 02:51.761
Reiji's always been really lucky.
Luck's the only thing he's got going for him!

02:52.131 --> 02:54.031
Hey, that's not nice!

02:54.031 --> 02:55.301
Please!

02:55.341 --> 02:58.071
Please fight me again!

02:58.371 --> 02:59.511
I...

02:59.511 --> 03:01.701
...I cannot afford to lose!

03:02.811 --> 03:03.831
Stop it!

03:04.041 --> 03:05.411
The outcome has already been determined!

03:05.911 --> 03:08.141
You're a warrior. Accept defeat like a man!

03:10.051 --> 03:11.041
Mukai.

03:11.951 --> 03:15.791
I was unable to save my mother.

03:16.661 --> 03:19.591
It would have been better
if I were killed out there.

03:23.031 --> 03:23.831
Mukai.

03:26.801 --> 03:28.471
Wait a minute!

03:28.471 --> 03:29.831
H-Hey!

03:32.371 --> 03:33.531
Leave him alone.

03:34.611 --> 03:36.011
It's just part of competition!

03:37.341 --> 03:41.011
If you went around pitying all the losers,
you'd have no time for anything else.

03:41.281 --> 03:42.111
Yes.

03:43.051 --> 03:44.381
By the way!

03:44.381 --> 03:47.251
The main thing is that you beat us.

03:47.321 --> 03:50.551
So we've got to do all we can
to make sure you become champions.

03:51.091 --> 03:51.691
Right?

03:51.691 --> 03:52.521
Ah, right.

03:53.361 --> 03:56.121
I will not give up on the Dragonite!

03:56.531 --> 03:59.501
I'll stick closely to the Ohzora team...

03:59.501 --> 04:01.171
...and steal it from them in the end.

04:01.171 --> 04:04.711
It sounds like the next match
is about to begin.

04:04.711 --> 04:06.431
The next match?

04:06.911 --> 04:08.001
With Taiyou!

04:08.211 --> 04:09.211
Yeah.

04:09.211 --> 04:12.511
If Taiyou's team wins, we'll face them next.

04:12.711 --> 04:14.741
It's not gonna be easy. After all...

04:15.321 --> 04:17.681
...they're the defending champions!

04:26.161 --> 04:27.191
Terrific!

04:27.191 --> 04:28.531
The match hasn't started yet.

04:29.401 --> 04:31.161
Wh-Why that's...

04:32.401 --> 04:34.201
What in the world's going on?!

04:34.201 --> 04:35.791
What are they doing in Rikyu?!

04:36.871 --> 04:38.371
Hikaru Himuro...

04:38.371 --> 04:39.901
...and Ichirou Sumishiba!

04:40.171 --> 04:41.871
Who's that other guy?

04:44.881 --> 04:47.611
B-Bastard!

04:51.391 --> 04:54.411
Where could Mukai have gone?

04:55.291 --> 04:57.881
And what am I doing
worrying about that guy?

04:58.291 --> 05:00.451
This is crazy. I quit.

05:03.431 --> 05:07.231
On second thought,
who'll take care of him if I don't?

05:10.771 --> 05:11.841
Well?

05:11.841 --> 05:13.201
What now? Who wants to do it?

05:17.241 --> 05:18.581
Do as you wish.

05:20.551 --> 05:22.451
Then maybe I'll do it.

05:22.721 --> 05:26.881
Well, whoever fights them, I doubt
it'll take longer than two or three minutes.

05:37.961 --> 05:39.121
Go get him, Tsubame!

05:42.501 --> 05:44.641
Huh? You sure you wanna attack me alone?

05:44.641 --> 05:47.631
I don't mind if the three of you
wanna fight me at once.

05:48.181 --> 05:49.041
Don't take me lightly!

05:49.441 --> 05:50.511
Okay, everybody!

05:50.511 --> 05:52.381
It's the moment you've been waiting for!

05:52.481 --> 05:53.881
Without further ado...

05:54.211 --> 05:55.651
...begin fighting!

05:56.181 --> 05:58.621
Go! Arashi Storm!

06:01.961 --> 06:03.051
Take this!

06:08.461 --> 06:11.301
That pattern's boring.

06:12.201 --> 06:14.131
Well, not that I care.

06:14.601 --> 06:15.501
Here I go!

06:26.211 --> 06:27.451
Incredible!

06:27.451 --> 06:31.881
The match has just begun, and Light Night's
Knight defeats Arashi Storm with one blow!

06:37.221 --> 06:37.921
Wow.

06:44.531 --> 06:46.001
I'm your next opponent!

06:47.001 --> 06:47.861
Here I go!

06:53.871 --> 06:56.381
What an interesting trick.

06:56.381 --> 06:57.371
However...

07:15.261 --> 07:17.601
He's strong! Unbelievably strong!

07:17.601 --> 07:20.131
After taking care of Arashi Storm...

07:20.131 --> 07:23.691
...Light Night's Knight has also defeated
Renju's Namito Ryusi with a single shot!

07:25.271 --> 07:26.361
One more.

07:27.371 --> 07:28.841
Lai-Lai Cocoon!

07:39.921 --> 07:41.511
Here I go! Ranyokugen!

07:44.191 --> 07:45.621
You won't defeat me with that same trick!

07:48.861 --> 07:51.131
Hey! You're pretty good!

08:05.081 --> 08:06.151
Taiyou!

08:06.151 --> 08:07.081
Get him!

08:12.391 --> 08:15.051
Well, you're not the defending champion
for nothing. However...

08:23.761 --> 08:25.831
Then what about this?

08:25.831 --> 08:26.821
Shasenko!

08:29.801 --> 08:30.791
Tsubame!

08:48.021 --> 08:48.761
Amazing!

08:48.761 --> 08:51.781
Kouhei Toki and his Light Night's Knight...

08:51.931 --> 08:56.591
...have also defeated defending champion
Sun Wols with their overwhelming power!

09:00.171 --> 09:01.221
Taiyou!

09:01.701 --> 09:03.031
Th-This can't be.

09:03.371 --> 09:05.401
Hey! Where are you going, Reiji?!

09:05.571 --> 09:07.041
Too bad, isn't it?

09:07.041 --> 09:09.601
I've done some research on you
and found out...

09:09.911 --> 09:11.431
...you're overprotective of your teammates.

09:12.151 --> 09:13.581
What a fool!

09:13.581 --> 09:15.981
Placing unnecessary emphasis
on your teammates.

09:21.321 --> 09:23.221
Come on, Taiyou!

09:23.221 --> 09:24.361
Taiyou!

09:24.361 --> 09:26.661
Oh, no! Is he a friend of yours?

09:26.761 --> 09:28.031
That's too bad!

09:28.031 --> 09:30.531
You need to tell me these things sooner!

09:30.531 --> 09:32.671
If I'd known he was your friend...

09:32.671 --> 09:34.301
...I would've gone easier on him.

09:34.301 --> 09:35.131
What?!

09:35.501 --> 09:37.161
Don't be so upset!

09:37.371 --> 09:39.501
We're both from the same world, after all.

09:39.771 --> 09:42.261
What? Then you're from Earth, too?

09:42.681 --> 09:46.131
Well, this isn't the place
to ramble on about details.

09:46.551 --> 09:47.841
Now, then.

09:48.211 --> 09:50.441
To all the participants
of the Dragonic Heaven!

09:51.021 --> 09:52.511
Can you hear me?!

09:52.891 --> 09:54.851
I'd like to make a suggestion...

09:54.851 --> 09:57.521
...that would make
this tournament more interesting!

09:57.991 --> 10:02.301
How about, for tomorrow's match, our team
faces the remaining seven teams at once?!

10:02.301 --> 10:03.301
What?!

10:03.301 --> 10:04.661
What the hell are you saying?!

10:05.001 --> 10:06.561
Well, what I'm saying is...

10:07.331 --> 10:09.941
...since all the other teams seem so weak...

10:09.941 --> 10:12.671
...I'm offering to blow you away
all at once!

10:12.841 --> 10:15.431
- Sure, I'll take you on!
- We hafta teach you a lesson!

10:16.511 --> 10:18.141
Toki. We're leaving.

10:18.751 --> 10:19.441
Yeah.

10:33.791 --> 10:34.931
Okay, everyone!

10:34.931 --> 10:37.861
I'm looking forward to tomorrow's match!

10:41.601 --> 10:43.571
What in the world is going on?

10:44.041 --> 10:46.341
Why are those guys here?!

10:51.711 --> 10:53.581
So you've finally made your move...

10:53.581 --> 10:55.071
...Kouhei Toki.

11:01.291 --> 11:04.691
I imagine this upcoming game
is gonna be a lot of fun.

11:23.241 --> 11:25.051
Taiyou, you're awake.

11:25.051 --> 11:26.081
Miss Yukino?

11:26.081 --> 11:27.451
Where am I?

11:27.451 --> 11:29.851
You're in the hotel we're staying at.

11:30.381 --> 11:33.381
You sustained surprisingly minor injuries,
so we had you brought here.

11:33.621 --> 11:34.591
I see.

11:34.591 --> 11:36.951
So I must've fainted after that.

11:38.731 --> 11:41.061
Sorry we couldn't be of help.

11:41.531 --> 11:43.331
Tsubame. Renju.

11:44.301 --> 11:45.861
I'm glad you're okay.

11:46.371 --> 11:47.631
What's to be glad about?

11:47.631 --> 11:50.571
We caused you embarrassment
because we were weak.

11:50.771 --> 11:52.471
No, it's not your fault.

11:52.741 --> 11:54.871
We lost because I'm weak.

11:54.871 --> 11:56.011
That's all.

11:56.011 --> 11:57.341
That's not true!

11:57.841 --> 12:01.471
The most shameful is that Toki guy,
for using such cowardly tricks to beat you!

12:01.951 --> 12:03.541
Are you trying to cheer me up?

12:03.921 --> 12:05.821
You're such a kind person, Miss Yukino.

12:05.951 --> 12:07.791
R-Really?

12:07.791 --> 12:09.191
Well, I'm often told that.

12:10.191 --> 12:11.181
Where's Reiji?

12:11.521 --> 12:13.561
W-Well, he's out right now.

12:13.561 --> 12:16.291
He said something
about needing to find someone.

12:17.101 --> 12:21.091
Which reminds me,
we still haven't heard back from Daisuke.

12:21.431 --> 12:22.541
Man!

12:22.541 --> 12:24.971
Where are they, and what are they doing?!

12:30.141 --> 12:31.201
Found you!

12:32.011 --> 12:34.541
Hey, you seem a lot better than I expected.

12:36.521 --> 12:37.411
I've decided!

12:38.891 --> 12:39.891
Decided what?

12:39.891 --> 12:42.351
I will fight! One more time!

12:43.021 --> 12:44.461
What are you saying?

12:44.461 --> 12:47.631
I will challenge the champion
of the Dragonic Heaven to a bout!

12:47.631 --> 12:49.751
Then I will get the Dragonite.

12:50.201 --> 12:51.391
No matter what.

12:51.871 --> 12:56.001
I don't think it's likely for a champion
to accept a loser's challenge to fight.

12:58.371 --> 12:59.361
Kanper?

13:07.381 --> 13:08.051
Daisuke!

13:08.051 --> 13:10.041
Hey, are you all right?!

13:10.321 --> 13:11.891
K-Kyoji.

13:11.891 --> 13:13.581
What happened to you?

13:15.421 --> 13:16.581
A little something.

13:16.961 --> 13:19.721
I went for a visit to Guan-Coo's residence.

13:20.431 --> 13:21.621
I don't think they like me.

13:21.861 --> 13:23.301
Did you say Guan-Coo?!

13:23.301 --> 13:24.321
What were you doing there?!

13:26.901 --> 13:28.631
Wh-Why this is...

13:29.401 --> 13:33.641
I went to save this woman
who was confined by Guan-Coo.

13:33.641 --> 13:34.701
However...

13:35.381 --> 13:36.741
...I was too late.

13:36.741 --> 13:37.731
Wh-What?!

13:38.881 --> 13:41.111
Please. Give this to Mukai.

13:41.181 --> 13:42.771
H-Hey!

13:54.531 --> 13:57.991
I-It can't be true.

13:59.201 --> 14:03.101
Am I supposed to believe
that my mother died?

14:03.771 --> 14:05.331
Mother?

14:10.641 --> 14:12.411
Mother!

14:24.221 --> 14:25.561
Where did they go?

14:25.561 --> 14:27.221
Hikaru! Ichirou!

14:27.631 --> 14:29.361
And what are they doing in Rikyu?

14:38.811 --> 14:39.791
Hikaru!

14:44.811 --> 14:45.801
Hikaru!

14:46.051 --> 14:48.511
I've got a ton of things I wanna ask you!

14:49.081 --> 14:51.411
Why are you guys here in Rikyu?

14:51.551 --> 14:54.851
And why are you guys participating
in the Dragonic Heaven?!

14:55.361 --> 14:57.221
Because RI-ON told me to.

14:57.461 --> 14:58.461
RI-ON?

14:58.461 --> 15:01.021
Do you have any idea what bastards
the guys at RI-ON are?

15:01.561 --> 15:02.661
No.

15:02.661 --> 15:04.101
And I don't really care.

15:04.161 --> 15:05.231
What?!

15:05.231 --> 15:07.891
Do you remember that Dragon Drive battle?

15:15.411 --> 15:17.041
Yeah, I remember.

15:17.041 --> 15:18.071
So what?

15:18.581 --> 15:21.811
Although it was just for an instant,
you left me with a sense of fear.

15:24.081 --> 15:27.141
I've come here for one reason only.
To fight you.

15:38.971 --> 15:41.091
Long time no see, Meguru.

15:41.401 --> 15:42.941
I believe the last time we met...

15:42.941 --> 15:46.061
...you were still frequenting
the Dragon Drive Center.

15:46.571 --> 15:48.401
Boy, seeing you brings back memories.

15:48.841 --> 15:50.571
I knew you would come.

15:50.941 --> 15:53.381
I know exactly what you're after.

15:53.381 --> 15:55.521
Or rather, what your father's after.

15:55.521 --> 15:57.751
I know what Saizou Toki is trying to do!

15:57.851 --> 15:59.041
Hey, hold on.

15:59.421 --> 16:01.821
I'm in no mood for lectures.

16:02.161 --> 16:03.141
Meguru...

16:03.261 --> 16:04.921
...everything will be decided tomorrow.

16:05.191 --> 16:06.861
Do you have any idea what's going on?

16:06.861 --> 16:11.491
Your father is trying to get the Dragonite
for all the wrong reasons!

16:11.801 --> 16:13.771
And you're being tricked by him!

16:14.401 --> 16:17.401
At this rate, awful,
irreparable things could happen!

16:17.401 --> 16:18.771
Let me say this.

16:18.771 --> 16:22.371
I only understand about half
of what my father tells me...

16:22.781 --> 16:25.881
...and I can't even begin
to imagine what will happen...

16:25.881 --> 16:27.541
...if my father gets the Dragonite.

16:29.051 --> 16:31.181
But to me, what's important...

16:31.451 --> 16:34.111
...is the process along the way,
until I get the Dragonite.

16:34.491 --> 16:38.181
I only care about how to finally get it,
so that my dad can own it.

16:38.661 --> 16:39.651
You see?

16:40.331 --> 16:43.521
This is all a game
that my dad prepared for me.

16:44.101 --> 16:47.731
And I am the lead character in this game!

16:48.101 --> 16:49.431
A game?

16:49.841 --> 16:51.301
Are you serious?

16:51.571 --> 16:52.441
Yes.

16:52.441 --> 16:54.771
Everyone other than myself
is a mere pawn in the game.

16:55.041 --> 16:55.941
Pawn?

16:55.941 --> 16:57.641
Don't you see your teammates as friends?

16:57.841 --> 16:59.151
No way.

16:59.151 --> 17:00.311
Those guys?

17:02.151 --> 17:04.581
Hikaru's nothing but a battle geek!

17:04.751 --> 17:05.841
You're not getting it!

17:06.321 --> 17:09.721
I won't let anyone like you
get a hold of the Dragonite!

17:09.921 --> 17:11.691
Oh, no, I'm scared.

17:11.861 --> 17:13.851
I'd better watch out, then.

17:14.131 --> 17:16.931
I'll do my best not to lose tomorrow!

17:24.001 --> 17:25.511
To fight against me?!

17:25.511 --> 17:26.571
That's right!

17:26.571 --> 17:28.231
To fight against you!

17:30.111 --> 17:31.041
Chibi!

17:44.061 --> 17:45.051
Chibi!

17:49.101 --> 17:50.131
Why is it?!

17:50.131 --> 17:51.901
Why are you helping RI-ON?!

17:51.901 --> 17:54.871
RI-ON used Dragon Drive to trick us!

17:54.871 --> 17:57.891
They plan to conquer both Earth and Rikyu!

17:58.041 --> 17:59.201
So what?

17:59.411 --> 18:01.341
I'm interested in just one thing.

18:07.581 --> 18:09.281
Mugen-Iki.

18:22.031 --> 18:22.791
There!

18:24.661 --> 18:25.651
What?

18:41.651 --> 18:42.771
Damn you!

18:42.951 --> 18:44.421
Don't you realize?!

18:44.581 --> 18:46.851
If they get their hands on the Dragonite...

18:46.951 --> 18:49.561
...your family, friends, everyone at school...

18:49.561 --> 18:52.121
...everyone important to you could die!

18:52.961 --> 18:54.591
What do you think of that, Hikaru?!

18:54.991 --> 18:57.331
That has little bearing on me.

18:57.361 --> 19:00.561
Damn you, Hikaru!

19:31.601 --> 19:32.731
This is it!

19:32.731 --> 19:35.061
This is the kind of battle
I've been waiting for!

19:40.341 --> 19:41.601
What's so funny?!

19:41.971 --> 19:44.011
You're finally fighting against me seriously...

19:44.011 --> 19:45.101
...Reiji Ohzora.

19:45.181 --> 19:46.181
What?

19:46.181 --> 19:49.171
Is he saying that he wasn't fighting seriously
up until now?

19:52.921 --> 19:54.511
Okay, that's enough!

19:55.251 --> 19:56.381
Ichirou!

19:58.221 --> 19:59.781
You look banged up, Hikaru.

20:00.161 --> 20:03.131
Shall we say Reiji has the upper hand today?

20:03.131 --> 20:04.561
Look.

20:04.561 --> 20:08.431
While you two dimwits were preoccupied
with your emotional drama...

20:08.941 --> 20:12.671
...you never realized you were surrounded
by some mean-looking boys, did you?

20:12.671 --> 20:14.611
I knew it! You're the kids from earlier today!

20:14.611 --> 20:16.701
How dare you guys make fun of us?!

20:17.011 --> 20:19.001
I'll put an end to you right here, right now!

20:19.681 --> 20:21.481
What is it with those guys?

20:25.321 --> 20:26.581
Hey, wait, Hikaru!

20:26.851 --> 20:28.751
I'm not done talking to you yet!

20:28.751 --> 20:32.161
Boy, what a selfish guy
that Hikaru Himuro is.

20:32.291 --> 20:33.281
Get 'em!

20:35.191 --> 20:36.181
Hayate Slash!

20:42.671 --> 20:45.801
- Run!
- Help!

20:47.711 --> 20:51.311
You're not the only one
who's become stronger, Reiji.

20:51.311 --> 20:52.611
Ichirou.

20:52.781 --> 20:54.251
So you're with RI-ON, too.

20:54.411 --> 20:55.821
But why?!

20:55.821 --> 20:57.841
The guys at RI-ON are bad guys!

21:00.491 --> 21:01.151
Reiji...

21:01.151 --> 21:04.591
...in tomorrow's match,
be especially cautious of Kouhei Toki.

21:06.191 --> 21:07.961
Kouhei... Toki.

21:10.431 --> 21:11.421
Tomorrow.

21:16.441 --> 21:18.061
Tomorrow.

21:18.101 --> 21:19.001
Tomorrow.

21:22.441 --> 21:23.431
Tomorrow.

21:33.491 --> 21:34.481
Tomorrow.

21:56.381 --> 21:59.111
taikutsu datta
I was bored

21:59.111 --> 22:01.951
okubyou datta
I was a coward

22:01.951 --> 22:05.911
dareka wo jibun wo kizutsukete ita
I was hurting someone and myself

22:07.351 --> 22:10.121
tsuyogari itte
I tried to hide my weakness

22:10.121 --> 22:12.321
wagamama itte
I was being selfish

22:12.761 --> 22:16.891
doushiyoumonai kimochi mamoritsuzukete
Protecting the uncontrollable feeling

22:18.301 --> 22:20.971
otona ni natte
I became an adult

22:20.971 --> 22:23.701
kimi to deatte
Then I met you

22:23.701 --> 22:27.701
mune no sumikko yawarakaku natte
My heart got softened

22:29.011 --> 22:31.441
setsunaku natta
Longing for love

22:31.441 --> 22:34.451
dakishime atta
We embraced each other

22:34.451 --> 22:39.351
hakkiri mamorubeki mono wo mitsuketa
I finally knew what I wanted to protect

22:39.991 --> 22:42.721
tatta hitotsu no yuuki ga
Only one courage

22:42.721 --> 22:45.491
tatta hitotsu no kotoba ga
Just one word

22:45.491 --> 22:50.161
futari owaranai yume e to hakobu
Take us to an endless dream

22:50.861 --> 22:53.631
hon no chiisana yasashisa ga
Only a small kindness

22:53.631 --> 22:56.301
hon no wazuka na sasayaki ga
Only a small whisper

22:56.301 --> 23:00.971
futari wo sotto tsutsunde kureru
Wrap us gently

23:01.611 --> 23:06.201
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:07.111 --> 23:12.811
zutto konomama asa ga kurumade
Until the morning comes

23:15.251 --> 23:17.921
Next Episode

23:18.691 --> 23:20.591
The time has come for the final battle.

23:20.591 --> 23:24.051
I will do everything I can to win
the battle to protect the Dragonite!

23:24.961 --> 23:27.571
Right, and we now find out
about Rockaku's past...

23:27.571 --> 23:29.031
...and his ties with Kouhei Toki!

23:30.971 --> 23:31.601
What?!

23:31.601 --> 23:33.811
Mukai storms into Guan-Coo's residence...

23:33.811 --> 23:35.211
...and finds himself in trouble?!

23:35.211 --> 23:36.681
Close call!

23:36.681 --> 23:39.311
Next, on Dragon Drive, "The Catch".

23:39.311 --> 23:40.581
On another subject, Chibi...

23:40.581 --> 23:42.051
...is it just me, or are you talking now?

23:42.051 --> 23:43.651
The Catch
No way!

23:43.651 --> 23:44.841
The Catch
